{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Assignment Operators in Java"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use in assignment operators in Java."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Talk about principles, concepts, characteristics of general-purpose computer programming language in spoken and written situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on principles, concepts, and features of general purpose computer programming languages."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<span class= \"italic\">Used to </span> "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <b>Used to</b> for past actions that happen frequently in the past. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Let's take a look at the following structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<center>Subject+ <b>used to</b> + verb in base form + complement</center>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: </br><i>I<b> used to</b> teach assignment operators in class.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the negative form, we need to add the auxiliary <i>didn't</i>. So, the verb <b><i>used</b></i> takes the base form. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: </br><i> I <b>didn't use to</b> pass the exams of shortcut operators at university. </i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Similarly, when we want to use the interrogative form of the expression used to, we also have to use the auxiliary did."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:</br<<i><b> Did </b>you<b> use to</b> work with java when you were in college?</i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I used to work with Java very often, but now, I feel I don't understand most of its functions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Did you use to work with Multiplication and Division operations too?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Note: Be careful not to mistake <b><i>used to</b></i> with <b><i>be used to</i></b> or <b><i>get used to</b></i>; these other forms represent a habit in the present or a habit that someone is acquiring. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think I didn't use to work that much with divisions."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Assignment Operators and Shortcuts"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Assignment operator is the operator used to assign a new value to a variable. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Assignment operators is a kind of operator used in Java to manipulate variables. We can find the following ones: "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a = b \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Right operand is equal to left operand\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A += b\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A is equivalent to a + b.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A -= b\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A is equivalent to a -b.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A *= b \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A is equivalent to x times b .\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A /= b\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A is equivalent to b/a .\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A %= b \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A is equivalent to b%a.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hand in"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give something to someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I'm supposed to hand in a summary about Java assignment operators next week but I barely remember what they are."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "syntax "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "it is a set of rules that indicate how the elements in a system should interact"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you would like, I can explain to you how these operators work and their syntax.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "perform a mathematical operation "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to carry out the action of adding, subtracting, multiplying, etc. "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We perform the following mathematical operation: \u2018a = b + c'.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "remainder "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a number or value that is left over"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have to keep in mind that in Division, we can get a remainder when the result is not an even number."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shortcut "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the fastest way of form to accomplish something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I know there are also shortcuts in Java, would you help me remember what they are?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "put something into practice "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to practice or try something that you recently learned"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I would definitely put this into practice.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about other assignment operators in Java."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a poster in which you explain some characteristics and important details about the operators that you chose. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your poster with the rest of the class"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for information about other assignment operators in Java. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a poster, explaining important characteristics them"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share the poster with the rest of the class. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n5le02ob08re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<b>Louis</b>: Hey Catherine! I'm supposed to hand in a summary about Java assignment operators next week but I barely remember what they are. I used to work with Java very often, but now, I feel I don't understand most of its functions. </br>\n<b>Catherine</b>: Java isn't supposed to be difficult.  These assignment operators include mathematical operators that are used to give values to variables. If you would like, I can explain to you how these operators work and their syntax.  </br>\n<b>Louis</b>: That'll be great!"}, {"time": "32500", "image": "enpe7n5le02ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<b>Catherine</b>: Alright. The first two operators are Addition and Subtraction. As their names suggest, we use this operators to add or subtract value to a variable. I used to work a lot with these operations so I can give you a clear example. Imagine you have three variables with different values: \u2018int a = 10', \u2018int b = 5', and \u2018int c = 1'. Now we perform the following mathematical operation: \u2018a = b + c'.  Here, the value of \u2018a' is supposed to change from 10 to 6. We would follow the same process when we subtract.</br>\n<b>Louis</b>: I think I remember this. Did you use to work with Multiplication and Division operations too?</br>\n<b>Catherine</b>: For sure! These are supposed to be very common in Java. Let me give you a similar example. Take the following variables: \u2018int q = 15' and \u2018int t = 0'. Now let's perform the operation \u2018t = q/3'. Here, the value of \u2018t' will change from 0 to 5. However, you have to keep in mind that in Division, we can get a remainder when the result is not an even number. For instance, if I perform the following operation \u2018int n = 25/3', I will have a remainder equal to 1."}, {"time": "130800", "image": "enpe7n5le02ob08re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<b>Louis</b>: I think I didn't use to work that much with divisions. I don't remember ever having a remainder. I know there are also shortcuts in Java, would you help me remember what they are?</br>\n<b>Catherine</b>: Yes. These are operators which you can use to add or subtract 1 from a number. For example, we would use Increment and Decrement when we want to quickly increment or decrement a number by 1. If you want to increase or decrease the value of a variable by a value different from \u20181', use Plus-equals or Minus-equals. </br>\n<b>Louis</b>: I would definitely put this into practice. Thank you Catherine!"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n5le02ob08re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n5le02ob08re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can list the assignment operators used in Java. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can recall the syntax to use for different assignment operators in Java."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about shortcut operators and their use in Java."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "When do you think you have to use arithmetic operations in Java?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What Java functions do you know or have you worked with?  "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "What operators does Java work with?"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [3], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "STI", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Catherine and Louis go over Java-Assignment Operators."}], "type": "instructions"